# Plans workflow

* **Active plans:** keep under `.cursor/plans/` as `.mdc` files. Prefer descriptive names with a date prefix when useful, e.g. `2026-06-feature-name.mdc`. For `/worktask` streams, include the Task Number: `2026-08-T0036-short-slug.mdc`.
* **When a plan is fully executed or superseded:** move the file to `.cursor/plans/executed/` (keep the same filename so history stays traceable).

# Git workflow (feature / fix branches)

* **On work start:** create a dedicated branch from updated `main`, switch to it (SetActiveBranch), then implement.
  - **`/worktask`:** branch `T####-short-slug` (e.g. `T0036-wiki-search`). Follow [.cursor/skills/worktask/SKILL.md](../skills/worktask/SKILL.md).
  - **Ad-hoc (no Task Number):** branch `phase-N-short-slug` (legacy naming still OK).
* **On approval / “finish up”:** when the user says **finish up** (or equivalent approval to close the implementation), do all of the following in order:
  1. **Commit** any remaining work on the feature branch(es). If QA follow-ups shipped, name them in the commit message. **Bump app version** in this commit if it is not already on the branch — required for every finished Task ([versioning.mdc](versioning.mdc): MINOR +1 and PATCH `0` if this work added a new `drizzle/*.sql` file; otherwise PATCH +1; MAJOR stays `0` unless breaking). Increment from current `package.json`; do not re-count migrations. Set `createdAt` to UTC now. **In the same commit**, update repo-root [`RELEASE_NOTES.md`](../../RELEASE_NOTES.md): if the file is missing or empty (e.g. cleared after a GitHub release publish), recreate the standard stub header from that file’s documented format, then **prepend** a `## MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH — YYYY-MM-DD` block (UTC date of finish-up) with only the non-empty sections among Fixes / Enhancements / New Functionality / Breaking Changes / Deprecated Functionality. Each bullet is 1–3 sentences on **outcome**; schema or public API breaks go under Breaking Changes. Newest version blocks stay at the top. A future Build-release skill will consume this file for GitHub Release notes. **Also in that commit**, when this Task adds **major user-facing functionality** (new module, record type, reader, board type, or similarly website-worthy perk — not routine fixes or polish), update repo-root [`FEATURES.md`](../../FEATURES.md): add or revise single-line marketing bullets under the right section so the public feature list stays accurate. Skip `FEATURES.md` for bugfixes-only or internal/agent-workflow Tasks.
  2. **Merge** into `main` (ff-only when possible) and delete local (and remote if exists) feature branch(es) after merge.
  3. **Publish** — push `main` to `origin` (and any other remotes the repo normally uses).
  4. **Archive** the plan — move the active `.cursor/plans/*.mdc` into `.cursor/plans/executed/` (same filename), commit that move on `main`, and push again. Archived plan must include any QA follow-up notes.
  5. **Deploy to PROD** — from repo root on the app host, run `npm run deploy:prod` (install → migrate → `build:all` → restart `taskmesh` → health checks on `:3000` and nginx HTTPS → stamp `data/prod-release.json`). Confirm both health checks succeed before considering finish-up complete.
  6. **`/worktask` only** — after deploy succeeds: add a **completion Comment** on the PROD Task via API (include original scope **and** any QA follow-ups), set Task **state** to `complete`, and leave `dueDate` unchanged (see worktask skill).

# Delivery

* **End of every implementation pass:** provide a clear **QA checklist** for the user — step-by-step tests plus a short list of specific features to examine for approval or requested tweaks. Do **not** commit/merge/publish/archive until the user asks to **finish up** (or explicitly requests those steps).
* **QA follow-ups** (new functionality or corrections requested during QA): before treating the pass as done, do all of the following:
  1. **Update the active plan** — append a short “QA follow-ups” (or similar) section listing what changed and why.
  2. **Commit message** — when committing that work (or on finish-up), call out the QA additions/fixes explicitly (not only the original scope).
  3. **`/worktask` only** — post a PROD Task **comment** summarizing the QA changes (and include them in the completion comment on finish-up). See the worktask skill.
